            "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Pass the low-power signal to the 3D viewer**\n\nWhen a device is classified as low-end, this call still omits `lowPower`, so `Badge3DViewer` always receives its `false` default and starts the WebGL render loop instead of using its static fallback. Wire the existing `useDevicePerformance().isLowEndDevice` result into this prop, or perform the detection inside the viewer, so opening “3D 보기” does not impose the full renderer workload on devices the application already identifies as low-power.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n<!-- codex-code-review-finding:v1 -->"
